/target
__pycache__/
# Build output lands under the exec root, which is a sibling of the tree.
/target*
# ...and each standalone tool under tools/ has its own target directory, which
# the rooted patterns above do not match.
tools/*/target/
# Compiled probe binaries. The .c file is the evidence and IS committed; the
# binary is one `cc -O1` away. Built binaries are named without an extension, so
# a single pattern covers them all.
tools/*/probe/*[a-z0-9_]*
!tools/*/probe/*.c
!tools/*/probe/*.md
# Compiled test fixtures. Each is built by a one-line command that the test
# prints in its SKIP message when the fixture is absent, so committing the
# binaries would add megabytes and hide the fact that they are generated.
# The .c and .go sources stay: those are the fixtures.
tools/*/testdata/dnsfix
tools/*/testdata/cdyn
tools/*/testdata/iclient
tools/*/testdata/relayer
tools/*/testdata/srv
tools/*/testdata/ucli
# The two Go fixtures are directories holding their source plus one binary, so
# the binary is matched by name rather than by excluding the directory.
tools/*/testdata/gs/gs
tools/*/testdata/sg/sg
# Abstract and filesystem sockets the virtual network and the relay create.
*.sock